{"ts": 0.099368, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;97m2.2 — cd and the home folder\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[92mcd\u001b[0m changes your current folder.\r\n\r\n  \u001b[92mcd /tmp\u001b[0m       \u001b[90m# go to /tmp\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[92mpwd\u001b[0m           \u001b[90m# confirm you got there\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[92mcd\u001b[0m            \u001b[90m# go home (just 'cd' by itself)\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[92mcd ~\u001b[0m          \u001b[90m# also go home — ~ means $HOME\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nTwo more useful ones:\r\n  \u001b[92mcd -\u001b[0m          \u001b[90m# go back to the previous folder\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[92mcd ..\u001b[0m         \u001b[90m# go up one level (to the parent folder)\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[91mStages 1 and 2 start every practice prompt in\u001b[0m \u001b[94m/var/folders/jx/f_4n055973x5cwnyh_mhlw9h0000gn/T/shelltutor-sim-home-j14j9at7\u001b[0m\u001b[91m.\u001b[0m\r\nLater stages start in a stage folder inside it. If you wander off,\r\n\u001b[92mcd /var/folders/jx/f_4n055973x5cwnyh_mhlw9h0000gn/T/shelltutor-sim-home-j14j9at7\u001b[0m brings you back.\r\n\r\n\u001b[93m▶ Type \u001b[92mnext\u001b[93m to continue.\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 880}
{"ts": 0.099825, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 251}
